# Karpathy guidelines (cxado core)

Follow project [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and local **project overlay** rules. On errors: [core-kaizen.mdc](core-kaizen.mdc). Phase rhythm: [core-workflow-chain.mdc](core-workflow-chain.mdc).

**Tradeoff:** Caution over speed on non-trivial work.

## Four principles

| # | Principle | Practice |
|---|-----------|----------|
| 1 | **Think before coding** | Read master + phase plan; state assumptions; ask if scope unclear |
| 2 | **Simplicity first** | KISS; no speculative features beyond the phase |
| 3 | **Surgical changes** | Diff ⊆ phase plan; no drive-by refactors; critic rejects scope creep |
| 4 | **Goal-driven execution** | Phase DoD → named verify commands; loop until green |

Implementers on feature branches; **orchestrator chat = critic by default** ([core-parallel-branches.mdc](core-parallel-branches.mdc)).

## Before writing code

- Phase plan and branch name identified.
- Dependencies merged on `main`.
- Success checks listed with concrete commands.

Critic responsibilities and verdict format live in [core-agent-critic.mdc](core-agent-critic.mdc) — not restated here.
